<title>JAPAN: Bandai says will save $50 mln from planned merger.</title>
<headline>Bandai says will save $50 mln from planned merger.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bandai Co Ltd president Makoto Yamashina was quoted as saying on Monday that the company's planned merger with Sega Enterprises Ltd should &quot;easily&quot; save at least $50 million in costs.</p>
<p>Yamashina, who will become president of the new entity Sega-Bandai on October 1, gave his estimate during an interview with CNBC television network on Monday.</p>
<p>Asked how much the company can expect to save from the merger, Yamashina told CNBC, &quot;At least about $50 million, easily.&quot; He did not elaborate.</p>
</text>
